    "created_at": "2020-01-30T18:08:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-01-30T18:08:54Z",
    "body": "I've never been super happy about our whole sign extension story. In machine-independent space I think we're good, but we play very fast and loose in the machine-dependent space. Maybe there's some invariant we can use where we guarantee to only use the bits of a value that exist in its type. So there would be two effective `ANDLconst`s, one with a 32-bit type and one with a 64-bit type. `ANDLconst [-1]` could be removed in the former but not in the latter.\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
